/* Native timeline authoring inventory, version 1 .
 * Include with STATEMENT, PARAM, FORM and FAMILY defined; no include guard.
 * STATEMENT(id, word, section, once_rule, min_values, max_values, word_position)
 *   word_position is0 for headers,3 for ordinary events,2 for gen/lane.
 *   Counts exclude the word and event prefix; -1 means variable maximum.
 *   These are outer envelopes: native readers own discontinuous arities.
 * PARAM(id, statement_id, FIELD, position, type, lo, hi, unit, human,
 *       scale, clamp, default_value, mutable, depends, checker, choices, form)
 *   Position uses original zero-based line tokens. N+ repeats from N;
 *   N+.PART addresses packed route edges; N.KEY addresses key=value.
 *   Header word is token0; ordinary event word token3; gen/lane token2.
 *   Every event explicitly lists its time, stream and voice/ID prefix.
 *   lo converts to int64_t; hi to uint64_t. Nonnumeric rows use 0,0.
 *   Numeric bounds are accepted outer bounds, not effective engine clamps.
 *   Human numeric value is raw/scale (PLAN45); scale is a decimal divisor.
 *   Default prefixes disambiguate token: (optional-token omission),
 *   statement: (whole-statement omission), and initial: (runtime state before
 *   any event). required means no omitted value is supplied; context/external
 *   depend on the record/build or generator table. Defaults never determine
 *   arity and never enable a feature: native readers still require every
 *   operand of an authored statement, including statement:/initial: rows.
 *   mutable=1 means this field is set through an existing timeline event;
 *   0 makes no claim about a separate live application API or modulation.
 *   form=all unless an alternative token layout requires a selector.
 *   depends and checker describe existing native constraints; metadata does
 *   not itself validate names, arity, feature compatibility or coupled sets.
 * FORM(statement_id, form_id, selector_position, match_kind, values, checker)
 *   Describes canonical tokens already accepted by the native reader. It is
 *   not an authored-input validator. exact/prefix match pipe-separated values;
 *   count selects a full-line argc; default_or_exact selects an exact value
 *   or an omitted optional component, never an unknown supplied value.
 *   Prefixes match canonical stems (pitch0), not acceptance of pitchXYZ.
 *   A physical value has exactly one matching selector form; callers check
 *   that uniqueness rather than inventing fallback values. form=all rows
 *   are unconditional. Missing route means OPS2.
 *   The external generator position6+slot maps only selected GEN_PARAM
 *   p-slots: p0->6, p1->7, p2->8, p3->9. It does not consume other
 *   trailing tokens; Euclid PARENT is separately selected at last.
 *   SOURCE/TARGET enum rows own their whole textual token. Numeric suffix
 *   components are described in their choices/dependencies, not duplicate
 *   PARAM rows; packed route components instead each own their leaf.
 *   No parameter range or accepted timeline value is changed by this file.
 * FAMILY links the generator inventory once. Generator PARAM references
 *   map positions to that table; they deliberately repeat no numeric bounds.
 */


